text.section:
Upon request by the Virginia Parole Board related to an investigation and report conducted pursuant to this section and except to the extent otherwise permitted by law, all public bodies engaged in criminal law-enforcement activities shall provide copies of the following records:

Unredacted criminal investigative files, defined as any documents and information including complaints, court orders, memoranda, notes, incident reports, officers' field summary reports, diagrams, maps, photographs, video recordings, audio recordings, correspondence, narrative reports, witness statements, victim statements, the identification of witnesses and victims and their personal identifying information, prosecution files, photo lineups, and evidence relating to a criminal investigation or prosecution regardless of the juvenile status of the victim, witness, or suspect;


An attorney for the Commonwealth's prosecution files;


Records of any call for service or other communication to an emergency 911 system or communication with any other equivalent reporting system;


Adult and juvenile arrestee photographs taken during the initial intake following the arrest and as part of the routine booking procedure;


Information relative to the identity of any individual, to include a juvenile and his personal identifying information, who is arrested and charged, and the status of the charge or arrest; and


Sealed presentence investigation reports.
